  "title": "Ulugh Beg Observatory, Samarkand",
  "summary": "Ulugh Beg established an observatory on a rocky hill outside Samarkand in 1420; another source places its design and construction in the early 1420s under the scholar Jamshid al-Kashi. The circular building was about 46 m across and three storeys high, and housed the Fakhri sextant, of 40.04 m radius, set in a trench. Only the underground section survives.",
